# XSH isatty()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# isatty() on a terminal needs a pseudo-terminal, obtained with posix_openpt(),
# grantpt(), unlockpt() and ptsname() (XSI); tests that need none are Base.
# No test relies on the run having a terminal on its standard descriptors.
#
# "when BASE|XSI": the requirements are Base; XSI is named only so that the
# driver builds these tests with the XSI feature macro (the pseudo-terminal
# set-up needs it). They run wherever they build, and a set-up that is not
# available is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.isatty.001
anchor     functions/isatty.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isatty.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       isatty() on a descriptor for the subsidiary side of a pseudo-
           terminal (opened with O_NOCTTY) returns 1.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
test       t/001-pty-slave.c

assertion  XSH.isatty.002
anchor     functions/isatty.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isatty.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       isatty() returns 1 for a dup() of the subsidiary descriptor and
           for a second, read-only open of the same subsidiary device.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base.
test       t/002-pty-dup.c

assertion  XSH.isatty.003
anchor     functions/isatty.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       isatty() returns 0 (not 1, not -1) for descriptors of a regular
           file, a directory, both ends of a pipe, a socket and /dev/null.
note       errno is not examined: the page lets it be set or left alone.
test       t/003-not-terminal.c

assertion  XSH.isatty.004
anchor     functions/isatty.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/isatty.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       isatty() returns 0 for -1 and for a descriptor that has been
           closed.
note       errno is not examined: setting EBADF is optional.
test       t/004-bad-fd.c
